<asp:Content ID="Content3" ContentPlaceHolderID="ContentPlaceHolderMain" Runat="Server">
    <h1>Comparison to popular games</h1>
    <hr />
    <h2 id="GNOSIA-VS-Among-Us">GNOSIA VS Among Us</h2>
    <p>GNOSIA and Among Us are both social deduction games, but they differ in setting, mechanics, and player experience. Among Us is set in a space-themed environment where players work together to complete tasks while trying to identify the impostors among them. GNOSIA, on the other hand, is set in a sci-fi universe where players are trapped on a spaceship and must figure out who among them is a Gnosia, an alien parasite that can take over human bodies.</p>
    <div class="comparison-table-container">
  <table class="comparison-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Feature</th>
        <th>Among Us</th>
        <th>Gnosia</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Player Count</td>
        <td>Multiplayer (4-15 players)</td>
        <td>Single-Player (You vs. 14 clever AI characters)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Gameplay Style</td>
        <td>Real-time movement & mini-games</td>
        <td>Turn-based debates & visual novel storytelling</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Progression</td>
        <td>Casual party rounds (No carry-over)</td>
        <td>RPG leveling (Upgrade your charisma, stealth, and logic)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Story & Lore</td>
        <td>Minimal / Sandbox</td>
        <td>Deep, gripping sci-fi mystery with a time-loop narrative</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Play Session</td>
        <td>10-15 minutes per round</td>
        <td>Short 5-minute loops, perfect for quick sessions</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

    <p><strong>Why you should try it:</strong> Instead of relying on internet strangers, Gnosia forces you to learn the unique personalities, lies, and tells of 14 beautifully designed AI crewmates. Every time the loop resets, the roles change—making every round a brand-new puzzle to solve.</p>

    <h2 id="Constanc-VS-Hollow-Knight">Constanc VS Hollow Knight</h2>
    <p>Captivated by the tight platforming and atmospheric worlds of Hollow Knight. Constancetakes that beloved Metroidvania foundation and splashes it with a brilliant paint mechanic, where you use a paintbrush to dash through fluid transformations and traverse a decaying inner world.</p>
    <div class="comparison-table-container">
  <table class="comparison-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Feature</th>
        <th>Hollow Knight</th>
        <th>Constance</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Genre</td>
        <td>2D Metroidvania / Action</td>
        <td>2D Metroidvania / Action-Platformer</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Core Mechanic</td>
        <td>Nail combat and Soul spells</td>
        <td>Paintbrush attacks and fluid momentum dashes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">World & Theme</td>
        <td>A melancholic, ruined insect kingdom</td>
        <td>The vibrant yet decaying inner psyche of an artist</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Visual Style</td>
        <td>Gothic, atmospheric hand-drawn art</td>
        <td>Dynamic, colorful hand-drawn illustration</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Gameplay Focus</td>
        <td>Precision combat and exploration</td>
        <td>Fluid movement transitions and momentum-based platforming</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
    <p><strong>Why you should try it:</strong> Constance< perfectly captures the challenging, rewarding exploration of a great Metroidvania but introduces a refreshing sense of momentum. If you love the tight controls of <em>Hollow Knight</em> but want a game that transforms your attacks into a flowing, high-speed dance of paint and platforming, this is an absolute must-play.</p>
    
    <h2 id="Rivals-of-Aether-VS-Super-Smash-Bros">Rivals of Aether VS Super Smash Bros </h2>
<p>Hooked on the high-flying platform fighting of Super Smash Bros but looking for deeper competitive mechanics and limitless character options? Rivals of Aether takes the smash-style formula, tightens the combat for a faster pace, and unlocks infinite possibilities through its community-driven features.</p>

<div class="comparison-table-container">
  <table class="comparison-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Feature</th>
        <th>Super Smash Bros</th>
        <th>Rivals of Aether</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Visual Style</td>
        <td>3D Models & Cinematic Stages</td>
        <td>Beautiful, retro-style 2D Pixel Art</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Defensive Mechanics</td>
        <td>Shielding, rolling, and grabbing</td>
        <td>No shields or grabs! Focuses on a precise Parry system</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Stage Recovery</td>
        <td>Ledge grabbing and hanging</td>
        <td>No ledges! Uses wall-jumps and elemental saves</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Roster & Characters</td>
        <td>Massive, fixed roster of iconic gaming legends</td>
        <td>Tight core roster, each with unique elemental powers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Modding Support</td>
        <td>None (Official content only)</td>
        <td><strong>Steam Workshop Support</strong> (Thousands of community-made characters & stages)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p><strong>Why you should try it:</strong> Rivals of Aether is a dream come true for Smash fans who want a faster, more combo-heavy competitive experience without defensive options like shield-camping. But the absolute game-changer is the Steam Workshop integration. It allows you to effortlessly download and play as thousands of custom fighters—ranging from perfectly balanced original competitive characters to hilarious pop-culture icons.</p>

    <h2 id="Smack-Talk-VS-Brawlhalla">Smack Talk vs Brawlhalla</h2>
<p>Love the chaotic platform-brawling of Brawlhallaor Super Smash Bros, but wish you could literally scream your enemies off the stage? Smack Talk takes traditional platform fighting and powers it with your actual microphone. To charge your ultimate attacks, you don't just mash buttons—you have to spit out voice-activated one-liners!</p>

<div class="comparison-table-container">
  <table class="comparison-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Feature</th>
        <th>Brawlhalla</th>
        <th>Smack Talk</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Core Mechanic</td>
        <td>Standard controller inputs and weapon pickups</td>
        <td><strong>Voice-controlled abilities!</strong> Speak to charge attacks</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Visual Style</td>
        <td>Clean, 2D vector animations</td>
        <td>Dynamic 2.5D pixel art in a 3D environment</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Combat System</td>
        <td>Building damage to knock players off-screen</td>
        <td>Smash-style percentages, but driven by vocal hype</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Party Factor</td>
        <td>High (Friends yelling at each other on the couch)</td>
        <td>Absolute Chaos (The game literally <em>requires</em> you to yell at your friends!)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p><strong>Why you should try it:</strong> Smack Talk is the ultimate party fighter that bridges the gap between a traditional brawler and a hilarious social game. It completely changes the energy in the room when players are forced to scream epic or ridiculous one-liners into their mics just to survive. If you want a fighting game that guarantees non-stop laughter and perfectly captures the feeling of actual "smack talk", this indie gem is a must-play.</p>

    <h2 id="Checkmate-Showdown-VS-Traditional-Chess">Checkmate Showdown VS Traditional Chess</h2>
<p>What happens when you take the centuries-old strategy of <strong>Traditional Chess</strong> and smash it together with the high-octane combos of games like <strong>Street Fighter</strong>? <strong>Checkmate Showdown</strong> takes the ultimate game of the mind and turns it into a test of reflexes, where capturing a piece isn't guaranteed—you have to physically fight for it in a 2D arena!</p>

<div class="comparison-table-container">
  <table class="comparison-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Feature</th>
        <th>Traditional Chess</th>
        <th>Checkmate Showdown</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Core Genre</td>
        <td>Turn-based strategy board game</td>
        <td>Strategy board game meets 2D Fighting Game</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Resolving Captures</td>
        <td>The attacking piece wins automatically</td>
        <td>A real-time 1v1 fighting match decides who survives!</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Skill Requirement</td>
        <td>Purely tactical and forward-thinking</td>
        <td>Tactical planning AND fighting game execution (combos, specials)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td class="feature-name">Pacing</td>
        <td>Slow, methodical, and quiet</td>
        <td>A wild mix of strategic thinking and fast-paced brawling</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p><strong>Why you should try it:</strong> Checkmate Showdown is the ultimate brain-and-brawn mashup. It completely shakes up chess by giving you a fighting chance to save a blundered piece through sheer combat skill, while also adding a deep layer of board strategy to traditional fighting games. It’s competitive, hilarious, and a completely fresh take on two legendary genres.</p>
</asp:Content>

